        "timestamp": 1775467770,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. War in the Middle East: Donald Trump threatens to hit Iran power plants Middle East Issued on: 06/04/2026 - 11:29 Modified: 06/04/2026 - 11:29 Israeli strikes killed the intelligence chief of Iran's Revolutionary Guards, as the Islamic republic on Monday defied threats from US President Donald Trump to devastate civilian infrastructure if it does not reopen the Strait of Hormuz. 'Hit by both sides': US war on Iran threatens Iraq's 'careful strategy of multi-alignment' 06/04/2026 Middle East Middle East war: ‘No indication that legitimate US-Iran talks taking place’ 06/04/2026 Middle East Trump hails victory after US mission to rescue pilot from Iran 06/04/2026 Middle East War in the Middle East: Israel says residential building hit by Iranian missile 06/04/2026 Middle East War in the Middle East: Israeli strike on South Beirut kills at least 4 people 05/04/2026 Middle East War in the Middle East: the US rescues missing airman from Iran 05/04/2026 Middle East US war on Iran: Trump pressures allies in war effort but offers 'no role in strategy' 05/04/2026 Middle East French boats set sail from Marseille to join Gaza aid Flotilla 05/04/2026 Middle East \"We got him!\": US rescues aviator whose fighter jet was shot down in Iran 05/04/2026 Middle East"
